__2 Nearness, proximity; see अर्धदेव. (अर्ध may be compounded with almost every noun and adjective; as first member of compound with nouns it means 'a half of' and forms an एकदेशिसमास or तत्पुरुष; °कायः = अर्धं कायस्य; °पिप्पली, °मार्गः; °पुरुषः &c.; with adjectives, it has an adverbial force; °श्याम half dark; °भुक्त half eaten; so °पिष्ट, °पूर्ण &c.; with numeral adjectives it may mean either ‘a half of’ or ‘with an additional half’; °शतम् half of 100 i. e. 50; or अर्धेन सहितं शतम् i. e. 150; with ordinal numerals 'with a half or that number'; °तृतीयम् containing two and the third only half; i. e. two and a half; so °चतुर्थ three and a half. cf. अर्धं खण्डे समांशके [[Nm.]] 
-Comp. 
